// Specialization canary: two instantiations of one template must not share a
// body or a signature. Widths and results are deliberately asymmetric — a
// shared t8 specialization truncates 1000000, a shared t64 one misreads the t8
// call. Symmetric values would mask exactly this.
fnc: T <T> pick(a: T, b: T) { b }
s: t8 = pick(1, 100)
w: t64 = pick(2, 1000000)
print(s)
print(w)
